  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_017 (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.706 acc, a dramatic jump over all singleprofile configs (~0.53). The key untested question is whether avgpool is specifically important or whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) could further improve performance. config_025 is a clean single-variable comparison to config_017, changing only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, and weighted fusion constant. This is the best next experiment because: (1) it isolates the aggregation mechanism that appears to drive the largest performance gain observed so far, (2) the prior singleprofile data (config_009 vs config_024) showed fusion method has only marginal effect (~0.005), suggesting aggregation is the more impactful design axis to probe, and (3) the result generalizes—if transformer outperforms avgpool here, it likely does so across other encoder combinations, guiding all subsequent multiprofile experiments efficiently under the limited budget."
}

